      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(1,-1)$,$(3,-2)$,$(3,2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,-1)}=2(1)^{2}-3(-1)=5, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-2)}=2(3)^{2}-3(-2)=24, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,2)}=2(3)^{2}-3(2)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186172038/workspace/evidence/visual-repair/assets/f3ab58a4a45bb59cb31c8033f647eba7aa456fc885dfddf3539386b248adf8fe.png)",
